; Small programs and modules, each showing one thing an application does
; with the driver, for the documentation site: a page imports each file it
; shows whole, with ?raw, into Starlight's <Code>. They are built with the
; repository, so an example that stops compiling as the driver changes is
; found by the build and not by a reader. The programs need a Postgres to
; run; every other module is a piece of one, which a page shows alone.

(executables
 (names quick_start signing_in several_hosts pool listen)
 (libraries postgres-eio eio eio_main mtime ptime))

; @all builds only the modules a program links, and most pieces are linked
; by none, so @all asks for this directory's @check, which compiles every
; module.

(rule
 (alias all)
 (deps
  (alias check))
 (action (progn)))
